message.content:
Below is a **starter‑kit** you can copy into your own repo and grow at will.  
It’s written in **TypeScript**, uses **Node + Express** for the REST API, **Prisma** as the ORM (PostgreSQL), and a tiny **React** SPA for the UI.  

Feel free to drop the “weather” calls if you don’t need them – they’re just there so you know how to wire an external API such as [Open‑Meteo](https://open-meteo.com).

---

## 1️⃣ Project layout

```
tms-system/
├─ .env                # secrets & db url
├─ package.json
├─ tsconfig.json
├─ prisma/
│  ├─ schema.prisma
│  └─ migrations/
└─ src/
   ├─ api/
   │  ├─ v1/
   │  │  ├─ routes.ts          # all endpoints
   │  │  ├─ middleware/
   │  │  │  └─ auth.middleware.ts
   │  │  └─ validators/
   │  │       └─ shipment.validator.ts
   │  └─ index.ts              # express bootstrap
   ├─ domain/
   │  ├─ entities/
   │  │  ├─ Driver.ts
   │  │  ├─ Truck.ts
   │  │  ├─ Shipment.ts
   │  │  └─ Route.ts
   │  ├─ services/
   │  │  ├─ DriverService.ts
   │  │  ├─ TruckService.ts
   │  │  ├─ ShipmentService.ts
   │  │  └─ WeatherService.ts
   │  └─ repos/
   │        ├─ DriverRepo.ts
   │        ├─ TruckRepo.ts
   │        ├─ ShipmentRepo.ts
   │        └─ RouteRepo.ts
   ├─ infra/
   │  ├─ prismaClient.ts
   │  └─ logger.ts
   ├─ app.ts                  # main entry point
   └─ shared/
        ├─ errors.ts
        └─ types.d.ts
└─ public/                    # static assets / react build output
```

> ⚡️ *Why this shape?*  
> • `domain` keeps business logic isolated from infrastructure.  
> • `infra/prismaClient.ts` gives us one place to configure the DB connection.  
> • `api/v1/routes.ts` holds only routing glue – everything else lives in services/repositories.

---

## 2️⃣ Database Schema (`prisma/schema.prisma`)

```prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

/*
  Core entities needed for most TMS features
*/
model Driver {
  id           Int            @id @default(autoincrement())
  firstName    String
  lastName     String
  licenseNumber String         @unique
  phone        String?
  email        String?        @unique
  createdAt    DateTime       @default(now())

  trucks       Truck[]
  assignments  Assignment[]   @relation(name:"DriverAssignments")
}

model Truck {
  id             Int            @id @default(autoincrement())
  plateNumber    String         @unique
  make           String
  model          String
  year           Int
  capacityTons   Float
  vin            String?        @unique
  currentLocation Location?

  driverId       Int?
  driver         Driver?        @relation(fields:[driverId], references:[id])

  assignments    Assignment[]   @relation(name:"TruckAssignments")
}

enum StopStatus { PENDING IN_TRANSIT COMPLETED CANCELLED }

model Stop {
  id          Int          @id @default(autoincrement())
  address     String
  city        String
  state       String
  zipCode     String
  country     String
  arrivalETA  DateTime?
  departureETD DateTime?
  status      StopStatus   @default(PENDING)
  sequenceNo  Int

  shipmentId  Int
  shipment    Shipment     @relation(fields:[shipmentId], references:[id])
}

model Shipment {
  id               Int          @id @default(autoincrement())
  reference        String       @unique
  description      String?
  weightKg         Float
  volumeCubicMeters Float
  pickupAddress    String
  deliveryAddress  String
  scheduledPickup  DateTime
  scheduledDelivery DateTime
  actualPickup     DateTime?
  actualDelivery   DateTime?
  status           ShipmentStatus @default(SCHEDULED)

  truckId          Int?
  truck            Truck?        @relation(fields:[truckId], references:[id])

  stops            Stop[]

  createdAt        DateTime      @default(now())
  updatedAt        DateTime      @updatedAt
}

enum ShipmentStatus { SCHEDULED ASSIGNED EN_ROUTE DELIVERED CANCELED }

/*
  Simple assignment table linking drivers/trucks to shipments
*/
model Assignment {
  id          Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  driverId    Int
  truckId     Int
  shipmentId  Int
  assignedAt  DateTime @default(now())

  driver     Driver   @relation(fields:[driverId], references:[id], name:"DriverAssignments")
  truck      Truck    @relation(fields:[truckId], references:[id], name:"TruckAssignments")
  shipment   Shipment @relation(fields:[shipmentId], references:[id])
}
```

Run `npx prisma migrate dev --name init` after setting `DATABASE_URL`.

