## 7️⃣ Frontend Skeleton (React)

Install dependencies: `npm i axios react-router-dom@6`. Then:

```tsx
/* src/App.tsx */
import { BrowserRouter as Router, Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom';
import ShipmentsPage from './pages/ShipmentsPage';
import LoginPage from './pages/LoginPage';

function App() {
  return (
    <Router>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/login" element={<LoginPage />} />
        <Route path="/" element={<ShipmentsPage />} />
      </Routes>
    </Router>
  );
}

export default App;

/* src/pages/ShipmentsPage.tsx */
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

interface Shipment {
  id: number;
  reference: string;
  status: string;
  // ...
}

export default function ShipmentsPage() {
  const [list, setList] = useState<Shipment[]>([]);
  useEffect(() => {
    axios.get('/api/v1/shipments').then(r => setList(r.data));
  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      <h1>Shipments</h1>
      <ul>{list.map(s => (<li key={s.id}>{s.reference}</li>))}</ul>
    </>
  );
}
```

Serve the built bundle under `/public`, or run concurrently with the API during development.

---

## 8️⃣ Running locally

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# edit DATABASE_URL=postgresql://… and JWT_SECRET=…
docker compose up -d postgres
pnpm install
pnpm prisma generate
pnpm prisma migrate deploy
pnpm start   # starts node + express
cd ui && pnpm install && pnpm dev   # runs react dev server
```

Your API will now live at `http://localhost:3000/api/v1/...` and the UI at `http://localhost:5173/`.

---

## 🎯 What’s left out?

| Feature | Why omitted |
|---------|-------------|
| Auth/JWT | Boilerplate – plug in Passport or Fastify‑JWT |
| WebSocket for GPS streaming | Requires Redis/PubSub setup |
| Advanced route optimisation | Integrate Mapbox Directions or GraphHopper |
| Billing/invoicing | Separate microservice or module |

Add those pieces incrementally—each follows the same pattern shown above.

Happy coding! 🚚💨
